ASDMA-29/28l2022-DRR - ASDMA-Assam State Disaster Management
SEC also took note of the steps taken by ASDMA for setting up of a PMU forimplementation of same.54. 25: Approval of Rs. 313.69 Cr. under National Disaster RespondFund (NDRF) based on the flood memorandum submitted by theGovernment of Assam for the year 2024Resolution: SEC took note about the amount of Rs. 3L3.69 Cr. approved bythe High Level Committee chaired by the Hon'ble Union Home Minister oflndia under National Disaster Respond Fund (NDRF) as financial assistanceagainst flood damage of 2024.54. 26= Direction of SEC on other issues discussed with permissionfrom the Chair.
1. Revenue & DM Department to take up the matter with the Financedepartment and Accountant General, Assam regarding interest amountaccrued from State Disaster Response Fund (SDRF) and State DisasterMitigation Fund (SDMF) to be refunded to the Government of lndia. Furtherimmediate steps to be taken for release of pending installments under SDMF.2. Water Resources Department informed that the department could not obtainvetting from Central Water Commission (CWC) on 48 proposals amounting toRs. 511.83 for erosion protection works under XV FC and therefore, thedepartment has now submitted 9 fresh proposals for River Erosion Mitigationworks vetted by CWC Regional Office, Guwahati and TAC of the departmentamounting to Rs. 191.4L Cr.The SEC took note of the same.
3. ASDMA to examine and process the proposal submitted by Civi! Defence &Home Guards for procurement of electrical sirens and other Search & RescueEquipments.
The meeting ended with a vote of thanks from the Chair.Digitally signed byRAVI KOTADate: L4-10-20252L:46:55
