ASDMA-29,/28l2O22-DRR - ASDMA-Assam State Disaster Management
l/ 1277 642 / ?Ozs
Disaster Management Rules 2010 enabling State Disaster ManagementAuthority to make regulations governing the service conditions of ASDMAemployees as notified vide ECF. 250L46194 dated the July 8, 2024.54. 2O: Approval of State Executive Committee (SEC) on the revisionof existing Terms of Reference (ToR) of lnformation Assistantsengaged in SEOC and DEOC.Resolution: SEC approved the revised Terms of Reference (ToR) oflnformation Assistants engaged in SEOC and DEOC as placed at Annexure-xl.
54. 2L= Approval for procurement of 2O lnflatable Rubber Boats withOBM (engine) by the Fire & Emergency Services, Assam fordeployment in the urban areas of Assam during water logging andurban flooding.Resolution: SEC approved an amount of Rs. L,34,90,000/- for procurementof 20 lnflatable Rubber Boats with OBM (engine) by the Fire & EmergencyServices, Assam.SEC also directed Fire & Emergency Services / State Disaster Response Forceto keep the boats at various strategic locations of the State.SEC further directed the Fire & Emergency Services to assess if some existingboats need to be decommissioned and replenished.54. 22: Urban Flood Risk Management Programme for Guwahati Cityunder National Disaster Mitigation Fund (NDMF).Resolution: SEC took note about the amount of Rs. 222.22 Cr. approved bythe High Level Committee chaired by the Hon'ble Union Home Minister oflndia for Urban Flood Risk Management Programme for Guwahati City underNational Disaster Mitigation Fund (NDMF).SEC also directed DoHUA to take urgent necessary steps for implementationof measures proposed under this programme in coordination with ASDMA.Funding would be from MHA through ASDMA.54. 231 Restoration and Rejuvenation of wetlands of Assam underNational Disaster Mitigation Fund (NDMF).Resolution: SEC took note about the amount of Rs. 692.05 Cr. approved bythe High Level Committee chaired by the Hon'ble Union Home Minister oflndia for Restoration and Rejuvenation of 15 wetlands of Assam to beimplemented by Water Resources Department.SEC also directed Water Resources Department to take necessary steps forimplementation of measures proposed under this allocation in coordinationwith ASDMA .54. 24:. Approval of fund under National Disaster Response Fundbased on PDNA repoft submitted by the Government of AssamResolution: SEC took note about the amount of Rs. L270.788 Cr. approvedby the High Level Committee chaired by the Hon'ble Union Home Minister oflndia for implementation of measures as per the PDNA report.

