ASDMA-29/28l2o22-DRR - ASDMA-Assam State Disaster Management
the newly constructed District Emergency Operation Centre (DEOC) buildingin DC Office of Kokrajhar, Majuli and Golaghat district.54. 1O: Approval of fund amounting to Rs. 14.12913 Lakh to bereleased to the District Commissioner , Cachar from the H/A 2245-02-LOL-47O3-OOO-32-O1-SOPD-GSP (GR-Flood) for repair of steel boatunder lnland Water Transport Division, Silchar.Resolution: SEC approved an amount of Rs. L4.l-2913 Lakh to be releasedto the District Commissioner, Cachar from the H/A 2245-02-LO].-4703-000-32-0L-SOPD-GSP (GR-Flood) for repair of steel boat under lnland Water TransportDivision, Silchar.SEC also directed ASDMA to take up with IWT regarding requirement of steelboats for Sribhumi and Cachar Districts.
54. 11: Approval of fund amounting to Rs. 3.99471 Lakh submittedby District Commissioner, Barpeta against renovation of Officers'Club, Barpeta for accommodating NDRF Team during Flood ReliefOperation, 2023Resolution: SEC approved an amount of Rs. 3.9947L Lakh for makingpayment from the SDRF for renovation of Officers' CIub, Barpeta foraccommodating NDRF Team during Flood Relief Operation,2023.SEC, however, directed the Revenue & DM Department to put on record theduration of stay of the NDRF team during flood rescue operation in Barpetaduring 2023 while releasing the amount.54. L2= Ex post facto approval to three projects under SDRFexecuted by the Water Resources Department in Majuli in the year2022-23 amounting to Rs. 553.35 LakhsResolution: SEC accorded ex-post facto approval to the following threeprojects executed under SDRF by the Water Resources Department in Majuliin the year 2022-23 amounting to Rs. 553.35 Lakhs.1. lmmediate measures for restoration of flood damaged river bank atMajorchapori area of Subansiri River under SDRF for the year 2022-23(Rs. 209.00 Lakhs)2. lmmediate measures for restoration of flood damaged river bank atBordoti Erasuti, Chengelisuti , 2 no. Missamora and Fengsuighuli area ofSubansiri river under SDRF for the year 2022-23 (Rs. L24.35 Lakhs)3. lmmediate measures for restoration of flood damaged of river bank u/sof Chengelisuti and d/s of Fengsuighuli of river Subansiri in Majuli underSDRF for 2022-23 (Rs. 220.00 Lakhs)SEC however, directed the Water Resource Department to ensure that theworks executed under the above projects are surviving and joint verificationis done by the Department with representatives from DDMA Majuli andASDMA before releasing the fund.54. 13: Ex Post Facto approval of fund released to ASDMA for RGFlood DBT Resolution: SEC accorded ex post facto approval for an amountof Rs. 838.L719L lakhs released by the Revenue & DM Department to ASDMA
