ASDMA-29,/28I2o22-DRR - ASDMA-Assam State Disaster Management
l/ 127 7 542 / 2025
54.4 Approval for 3O nos. of SDRF Proposals of Flood / Stormdamaged Schools pertaining to Department of School Education forthe year 2024-2025Resolution: SEC approved 30 SDRF proposals of the Department of SchoolEducation, Assam for the year 2024-2025 for an amount of Rs. 43.19 Lakhsfor repair / restoration of 30 schools damaged due to flood / storm for theyear 2024-25 as placed at Annexure-lll.54. 5: Approval of SDRF proposals of lrrigation Department for theyear 2024-25Resolution: SEC approved 7 SDRF proposals of lrrigation Department for theyear 2024-2025 for an amount of Rs. 13.50 Lakhs as placed at Annexure-lV.54. 6: Approval of SDRF proposals of PWD Roads Department for theyear 2022-23Resolution: SEC approved 3L SDRF proposals of Public Works RoadsDepartment for the year 2022-23 for an amount of Rs. 67.40 Lakhs as placedat Annexure-V.
54. 7: Approval of SDRF Proposals of Power DepartmentResolution: SEC approved 46 SDRF proposals for immediate restoration ofLT lines, poles and Transformers damaged due to storm amounting to Rs.2,55,93,470 l- under Charaideo and Udalguri Electrical Sub-Divisions inCharaideo and Udalguri districts for the year 2024-25 and 2023-24 as placedat Annexure-Vl.
54. 8: Approval to the study on lntegrated geo-environmentalappraisal of Barpeta town, Howli town, Barpeta Road and itsadjoining area to assess the causes and remedies of urban flood.Resolution: SEC approved the proposal for the study on lntegrated geo-environmental appraisal of Barpeta town, Howli town, Barpeta Road and itsadjoining area to assess the causes and remedies of urban flood to be self-financed by GSl, NlH.
SEC also approved an amount of Rs. 46,34,9751- for the study to be borne byASDMA for contingency fund support and LIDAR study support from ASDMAfrom the balance fund available from the already completed project"Participatory awareness campaign on Disaster Preparedness & Door to Doorcampaign on flood safety and block wise street play on awareness of womenon DM".
SEC, further, directed ASDMA to take onboard the Department of Housing andUrban Affairs (DoHUA), Assam for the study.54. 9: Supply of furniture, electricals items and lnstallation of filterwith water storage tank at newly constructed District EmergencyOperation Centre (DEOC) building in DC Office of Kokrajhar, Majuliand Golaghat districtResolution: SEC approved an amount of Rs. 22,25,4551- for Supply offurniture, electricals items and lnstallation of filter with water storage tank at

